.TH MKINITRAMFS 8 "2026-07-15" "mkinitramfs" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mkinitramfs \- generate an initramfs image for Linux systems and LiveCDs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkinitramfs \fR[\fIoption\fR] [\fIargument\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmkinitramfs\fP generates an initial RAM filesystem (initramfs) image
containing the files, kernel modules, and binaries needed to boot a Linux
system.  It is inspired by Arch Linux's \fBmkinitcpio\fP but is intentionally
simpler.
.PP
The script builds the image in a temporary directory, runs a series of
build hooks to populate it, then archives the result with \fBcpio\fP(1)
and compresses it.  The generated image is an archive that the kernel
decompresses into a \fBtmpfs\fP at boot time; the \fBinit\fP script inside
then mounts the real root filesystem and hands off execution via
\fBswitch_root\fP(8).
.PP
Must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR \fIversion\fR
Use a custom kernel version instead of the running kernel
(default: output of \fBuname \-r\fP).
The corresponding directory \fI/usr/lib/modules/\fP\fIversion\fP must exist.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput\fR
Write the resulting image to \fIoutput\fR instead of the default
\fIinitrd\-\fP\fIversion\fP\fI.img\fP in the current directory.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR \fIinit\fR
Use a custom init script instead of the default
\fI@DATA_DIR@/init.in\fP.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR
Use a custom configuration file instead of \fI@SYSCONFDIR@/mkinitramfs.conf\fP.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR \fIcompression\fR
Compression format for the output image.  Supported values:
.RS
.TP
\fBgzip\fP
gzip compression (default).
.TP
\fBxz\fP
xz compression; \fBxz\fP(1) must be installed.
.TP
\fBzstd\fP
zstd compression; \fBzstd\fP(1) must be installed.
.TP
\fBlz4\fP
lz4 compression; \fBlz4\fP(1) must be installed.
.TP
\fBnone\fP
No compression; output is a plain cpio archive.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-m\fR \fImodules\fR
Comma-separated list of extra kernel modules to include.
Each module name is passed to \fBmodinfo\fP(8) for resolution; dependencies
and firmware are pulled in recursively.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR \fIbinaries\fR
Comma-separated list of extra binaries to include.  Each binary is resolved
via \fBPATH\fP, and its shared library dependencies (found with \fBldd\fP(1))
are included automatically.  Symlinks are followed.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR \fIfiles\fR
Comma-separated list of extra files to include.  Paths must be absolute.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR \fIhooks\fR
Comma-separated list of hooks to add \fBbefore\fP the hooks defined in
\fBHOOKS\fP.  These run earliest and take precedence over \fB\-a\fP, \fB\-s\fP,
and the configured \fBHOOKS\fP.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR \fIhooks\fR
Comma-separated list of hooks to add \fBafter\fP the hooks defined in
\fBHOOKS\fP (but after any hooks skipped by \fB\-s\fP).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR \fIhooks\fR
Comma-separated list of hooks to skip (remove from \fBHOOKS\fP before
adding \fB\-a\fP or \fB\-A\fP hooks).
.TP
\fB\-q\fR
Quiet mode.  Suppresses informational messages and non-fatal warnings.
Errors (\fBmsgerr\fP) are always printed.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Print a brief usage summary and exit.
.SH HOOKS
Hooks are the primary extension mechanism.  Each hook is a shell script
that is sourced twice:
.IP \(bu 2
At \fBbuild time\fP, to populate the initramfs with files, binaries, and
kernel modules via helper functions.
.IP \(bu
At \fBboot time\fP (inside the initramfs), to perform early userspace tasks
such as device discovery, decryption, or udev startup.
.PP
A hook file may define any of these functions:
.TP
\fBbuild_hook()\fP
Called during image generation.  Uses the \fBadd_binary\fP, \fBadd_module\fP,
\fBadd_file\fP, \fBadd_dir\fP, and \fBadd_symlink\fP helpers to populate the
initramfs tree.
.TP
\fBrun_early_hook()\fP
Called inside the initramfs before the root filesystem is mounted.
Used for device discovery, LUKS unlocking, starting \fBudevd\fP, etc.
.TP
\fBrun_late_hook()\fP
Called inside the initramfs after the root filesystem is mounted.
.TP
\fBrun_cleanup_hook()\fP
Called inside the initramfs after late hooks, in reverse hook order.
Used for teardown (e.g., stopping udevd, cleaning up device nodes).
.PP
Hooks can also override the \fBmount_handler\fP variable with the
name of a function that mounts the root filesystem, replacing the
default \fBmount_root\fP behavior (used by \fBliveiso\fP for overlayfs mounts).
.SS Hook resolution
A hook name is resolved by searching \fBHOOKDIRS\fP
(default: \fI@HOOKS_DIR@\fP, colon-separated) for
a file named \fIname\fP\fB.hook\fP.  Absolute paths may also be used directly
(via \fB\-A\fP or \fB\-a\fP).
.SS Standard hooks
.TP
\fBautomod\fP
Auto-includes kernel modules for all currently loaded modules (reads
\fI/sys/module/\fP).
.TP
\fBbase\fP
Creates the essential directory layout (\fI/bin\fP, \fI/dev\fP, \fI/proc\fP,
\fI/sys\fP, \fI/run\fP, \fI/usr\fP, \fI/etc\fP), standard symlinks
(\fI/bin\fP \(-> \fI/usr/bin\fP, \fI/sbin\fP \(-> \fI/usr/bin\fP,
\fI/lib\fP \(-> \fI/usr/lib\fP, \fI/lib64\fP \(-> \fIlib\fP,
\fI/usr/lib64\fP \(-> \fIlib\fP, \fI/usr/sbin\fP \(-> \fIbin\fP),
and core binaries (shell, mount, \fBswitch_root\fP, \fBmodprobe\fP,
\fBblkid\fP, \fBsed\fP, \fBgrep\fP, \fBawk\fP, etc.).
.TP
\fBencrypt\fP
Adds LUKS encryption support: \fBcryptsetup\fP(8), \fBdmsetup\fP(8),
\fBlvm\fP(8), and the \fBdm_mod\fP kernel module.  At early boot prompts
for a passphrase and unlocks the LUKS device, then activates LVM volume
groups.
.TP
\fBmodules\fP
Includes kernel modules from common driver categories (block, SCSI, ATA,
USB storage, virtio, filesystems, crypto, etc.).
.TP
\fBudev\fP
Includes \fBudevd\fP(8) and \fBudevadm\fP(8), standard udev rules, and
\fBata_id\fP / \fBscsi_id\fP helpers.  Starts udevd at early boot and stops
it during cleanup.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI@SYSCONFDIR@/mkinitramfs.conf\fP
Default configuration file.  Defines compression format, default hooks,
and optional extra binaries, modules, and files.  See
\fBmkinitramfs.conf\fP(5).
.TP
\fI@DATA_DIR@/init.in\fP
Default init script placed at \fI/init\fP inside the image.
.TP
\fI@HOOKS_DIR@/\fP
Default hook directory.
.TP
\fI/tmp/mkinitramfs.\fP\fI$$\fP
Temporary build directory, cleaned up on exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The script sets \fBPATH\fP to \fI/usr/bin\fP internally.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
An error occurred (missing prerequisites, invalid arguments, etc.).
.SH NOTES
The script aims for POSIX shell compliance.  Do not introduce bashisms.
.PP
Destination paths passed to \fBadd_file\fP inside hooks must \fBnot\fP have a
leading slash \(em they are relative to the initramfs root.
.PP
Hook ordering in \fBHOOKS\fP determines both build-time and boot-time
execution order.  Cleanup hooks run in reverse order.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlsmkinitramfs\fP(1),
\fBmkinitramfs.conf\fP(5),
\fBcpio\fP(1),
\fBgzip\fP(1),
\fBbsdcpio\fP(1),
\fBswitch_root\fP(8),
\fBdepmod\fP(8),
\fBmodinfo\fP(8),
\fBinitrd\fP(4)
